cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LureBench: A Benchmark and Evaluation Harness for Detecting AI-Generated Fraud Lures"
message: "If you use LureBench in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahamed
    given-names: Imran
    email: immu4989@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7717-7480"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21631777"
repository-code: "https://github.com/immu4989/lurebench"
url: "https://github.com/immu4989/lurebench"
abstract: >-
  LureBench is a benchmark and evaluation harness for detecting AI-generated
  fraud lures across phishing, business email compromise, romance and
  pig-butchering typologies. It ships a distribution-matched corpus, detector
  baselines from keyword rules to LLM-as-classifier judges, and an adversarial
  layer of character-level and LLM-driven evasion attacks, scored on both a
  fraud task and a text-provenance task.
version: 0.8.0
date-released: "2026-07-27"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - phishing
  - large language models
  - machine-generated text detection
  - adversarial robustness
  - AI security
